# Full-profile provider arm as ONE env source: compose.full.
# yaml and the replica twin (compose.replicas.full.yaml) both load it via
# env_file — `extends` resolves against compose.slim.yaml only, so an inline
# block in the full overlay would leave the twin provider-less and a webhook
# whose adapter session rides replica B would get a typed `unsupported`
# receipt. Loaded ONLY under the full profile; slim stays provider-less.
# Forgejo AssignCapabilityId is research.analyze, not the literal
# analysis.summarize — the deterministic worker advertises
# research.analyze, so the interim assign EXECUTES and the completion comment
# closes the loop (same precedent as the Mattermost arm).
# Label-routed interim assign: an issue labeled ofac:coding routes the coding
# capability to the coding team's gateway instead of the global research lane.
# PrRequestCapability marks the capability whose completed manifest may carry
# prRequest/commentRequests (connector dispatch). The coding Work lives on
# team-coding: the manifest ledger team-scopes a work's artifacts, and the
# coding worker's fleet owns them.
Providers__Mattermost__Enabled=true
Providers__Mattermost__EndpointId=mm-adapter
Providers__Mattermost__Tenant=chat.localhost
Providers__Mattermost__SiteUrl=http://mattermost:8065
Providers__Mattermost__BotTokenFile=/provision/mm-bot-token
Providers__Mattermost__BotIdentityProbeUrl=http://mattermost:8065/api/v4/users/me
Providers__Mattermost__LinkHintText=Your Mattermost account is not linked to a Facilitator identity — send me a DM starting with /link to link it.
Providers__Mattermost__AssignEndpointId=gw.team-alpha
Providers__Mattermost__AssignCapabilityId=research.analyze
Providers__Forgejo__Enabled=true
Providers__Forgejo__EndpointId=forgejo-adapter
Providers__Forgejo__Tenant=git.localhost
Providers__Forgejo__SiteUrl=http://forgejo:3000
Providers__Forgejo__BotUserId=facilitator-bot
Providers__Forgejo__AssignEndpointId=gw.team-alpha
Providers__Forgejo__AssignCapabilityId=research.analyze
Providers__Forgejo__AssignRules__0__Label=ofac:coding
Providers__Forgejo__AssignRules__0__CapabilityId=coding.implement
Providers__Forgejo__AssignRules__0__EndpointId=gw.coding
Providers__Forgejo__AssignRules__0__Team=team-coding
Providers__Forgejo__PrRequestCapability=coding.implement
# Telegram: the chat-plane label-routing arm (many groups, one bot).
# ChatLabelRouting makes a mention's normalized labels select the rule's
# capability/endpoint/team exactly as a forge issue label does; an unmatched
# chat keeps the global pair. Chat image/file uploads arrive as artifact
# sourceRefs and ride work.assign inputs. BotUserId is set explicitly, NOT
# probed: ResolveBotIdAsync reads a root-level `id` from the probe response,
# but Telegram's getMe nests it under `result` — a probe would put vendor API
# shape into the kernel (neutrality law), and Providers__Forgejo__BotUserId
# is the explicit-form precedent. The section is committed Enabled=true with
# a placeholder bot id (manual steps in reference/README.md); the adapter
# itself runs only under the `telegram` compose profile, so an un-flashed
# stack simply never delivers telegram events.
Providers__Telegram__Enabled=true
Providers__Telegram__EndpointId=tg-adapter
Providers__Telegram__Tenant=api.telegram.org
Providers__Telegram__BotTokenFile=/provision/telegram-bot-token
Providers__Telegram__BotUserId=000000000
Providers__Telegram__ChatLabelRouting=true
Providers__Telegram__AssignEndpointId=gw.team-alpha
Providers__Telegram__AssignCapabilityId=research.analyze
Providers__Telegram__AssignRules__0__Label=ofac:coding
Providers__Telegram__AssignRules__0__CapabilityId=coding.implement
Providers__Telegram__AssignRules__0__EndpointId=gw.coding
Providers__Telegram__AssignRules__0__Team=team-coding
Providers__Telegram__LinkHintText=Your Telegram account is not linked to a Facilitator identity — DM me /link to link it.
